    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13171" root="(دمو or دمى)" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَامِيَةٌ</span></b> , (S, K,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَّةٌ دَامِيَةٌ</span>, (T, * M, * Msb,)
<i>A wound in the head that bleeds but does not
flow with blood</i> (T, S, M, Msb, K) <i>as yet:</i>
(M:) such as flows with blood is termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَامِعَةٌ</span>.
(T, Msb.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجَّةٌ</span>.]

